## STEP 4: DEVELOPMENT ENVIRONMENT SETUP

### Create Project Directory
SSH into the Pi, then run:
```bash
mkdir -p ~/thesis
cd ~/thesis
```

### Install System Dependencies
These are needed by the DHT22 sensor library and OpenCV:
```bash
sudo apt install -y libgpiod2 python3-libgpiod
sudo apt install -y libcap-dev
sudo apt install -y v4l-utils
sudo apt install -y libopencv-dev python3-opencv
```

### Install uv (Fast Python Package Manager)
```bash
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
source $HOME/.local/bin/env
```
Verify it installed:
```bash
uv --version
```

### Install Dependencies with uv
After copying the project files to `~/thesis/` (see Step 5), run:
```bash
cd ~/thesis
uv sync
```
This reads `pyproject.toml` + `uv.lock`, creates a `.venv`, and installs all locked dependencies in one command.

**To include optional extras:**
```bash
# When ADS1115 ADC arrives:
uv sync --extra analog

# When NB-IoT module arrives:
uv sync --extra nbiot

# For local web dashboard:
uv sync --extra dashboard

# Everything at once:
uv sync --all-extras
```

### Activate the Virtual Environment
uv creates the venv at `.venv/` (not `venv/`):
```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
```

### Alternative: Install with pip (if you prefer)
```bash
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Future: When ADS1115 ADC Arrives
```bash
cd ~/thesis
uv sync --extra analog
# Then change SOIL_SENSOR_MODE to "analog" in config/settings.py
```

### Create Project Structure
```bash
cd ~/thesis
mkdir -p src config logs data models
touch src/__init__.py
```

### Verify Installation
```bash
python3 -c "
import adafruit_dht
import cv2
import RPi.GPIO as GPIO
print('adafruit_dht OK')
print(f'OpenCV {cv2.__version__} OK')
print('RPi.GPIO OK')
print('All core dependencies installed successfully!')
"
```

### Project Structure
```
~/thesis/
├── .venv/                         # Virtual environment (created by uv sync)
├── pyproject.toml                 # Project metadata and dependencies
├── uv.lock                       # Locked dependency versions
├── requirements.txt               # Fallback for pip users
├── models/
│   └── your-edge-impulse-model.eim  # Edge Impulse model file
├── src/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── sensors.py                 # DHT22 + soil moisture (digital/analog)
│   ├── camera.py                  # USB webcam capture
│   ├── inference.py               # Edge Impulse model inference
│   ├── transmit.py                # Data transmission (WiFi/NB-IoT)
│   └── main.py                    # Main monitoring loop
├── config/
│   └── settings.py                # All configuration in one place
├── logs/                          # Runtime logs
└── data/                          # Saved sensor data and images
```
